  "title": "Support-Set Target Leakage in Relational Foundation Models during In-Context Learning",
  "summary": "This study investigates the problem of support-set target leakage in relational foundation models during in-context learning, where target-derived features from the support set are unavailable for the query. The research evaluates the impact, detection, and mitigation of this leakage across different relational configurations and task settings.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Support-set target leakage is defined as the failure mode when target-derived features are present only in the labeled support set during relational in-context inference.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The study evaluates 20 controlled target-derived features across 13 RelBench tasks and 5 relational ICL configurations.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The leakage effects vary across tasks and relational distances, with 0-hop and Full leakage producing the largest aggregate deviations from clean evaluation.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
